# Framework fabrication workspace layout

Read `.fabric/project-profile.yaml` → `project.repository_kind` first.

This repository **builds** the framework. It is **not** an installed client
project.

## What exists at the repository root

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `.fabric/` | Fabrication identity (`project-profile.yaml`, source manifest, logs) |
| `distribution/payload/.ai-team/` | Installable payload (constitution, schemas, contracts, templates) |
| `distribution/payload/seeds/` | Fresh-install seeds copied to client `.ai-team/` |
| `src/`, `adapters/`, `scripts/` | Implementation and CLI |
| `.cursor/` | Minimal fabrication overlay only (not client skills/agents) |
| `adapters/cursor/templates/.cursor/` | Client Cursor payload (installed target) |

There is **no** root `.ai-team/` directory. If you see one, it was created by
mistake — remove it and run `python scripts/ai-team/validate.py`.

## Do not run the client cycle here

- Do **not** run `/compile-project`, gate commands, Work Unit orchestration, or
  `scripts/ai-team/feedback.py` record / retrospective / export.
- Do **not** create `.ai-team/runtime/` or `installation-record.json` at the repo
  root.
- Framework work uses git branches (`renov/*`, `fix/*`, …), review, and tests —
  see [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).

## Observe installed-client behavior

- Reference fixture: `tests/fixtures/projects/clean/`
- Or: `python tools/install.py --target <separate-directory>`

## Wrong files to follow

- `adapters/cursor/templates/AGENTS.md` describes **installed clients**, not this
  repo. Use root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) here.
